## 2. Color tokens

Every text and background pairing below passes WCAG AA (4.5:1 or higher).

| Token | Hex | Use |
|---|---|---|
| `--color-coral` | `#FF5A3C` | Primary brand color. Primary buttons, hero blocks, key highlights |
| `--color-coral-deep` | `#C2361C` | Coral text and links on light backgrounds (5.2:1 on cream) |
| `--color-sun` | `#FFD23F` | Secondary bright. Milestones, badges, highlights |
| `--color-cobalt` | `#2D4BFF` | Cool accent. Charts, tags, secondary actions, info |
| `--color-ink` | `#1A1A1A` | Primary text, dark surfaces, text on coral and sun |
| `--color-ink-soft` | `#5C5650` | Secondary text, captions |
| `--color-cream` | `#FFF8F0` | App background in light mode |
| `--color-white` | `#FFFFFF` | Cards on cream |
| `--color-line` | `#EADFD3` | Borders, dividers |
| `--color-success` | `#1F7A4D` | Confirmations, "on track" |
| `--color-warning` | `#B54708` | Needs attention soon |
| `--color-danger` | `#C0262D` | True alerts only, such as "Call your clinic now" |

Rules:

- Text on coral is always ink (`#1A1A1A`). White on coral fails contrast at 3.1:1; ink on coral passes at 5.6:1.
- Text on sun is ink. Text on cobalt is white.
- Normal lab values and routine info never use red.
- One bright (coral or sun) dominates a screen at most. Cobalt is for data and small accents.
- Medication, results, and billing screens use cream or white backgrounds with ink text. Brights appear only on one CTA or a small tag.

