## 3. Typography

Load from Google Fonts:

```html
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Bricolage+Grotesque:opsz,wght@12..96,600;12..96,800&family=DM+Sans:opsz,wght@9..40,400;9..40,500;9..40,700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
```

- Headlines use Bricolage Grotesque at weight 800 for big moments and 600 for section titles, with `letter-spacing: -0.02em`. Write headlines in sentence case or lowercase, never all caps.
- Body and UI text use DM Sans at 400, 500, or 700.
- Every number (doses, times, follicle sizes in mm, dollar amounts) uses `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums`. Doses are large enough that 150 IU can't be misread as 1.50.

| Style | Font | Size / line-height | Weight |
|---|---|---|---|
| Display | Bricolage | 40 / 44 | 800 |
| H1 | Bricolage | 32 / 36 | 800 |
| H2 | Bricolage | 24 / 30 | 600 |
| H3 | DM Sans | 18 / 24 | 700 |
| Body | DM Sans | 16 / 24 | 400 |
| Small | DM Sans | 14 / 20 | 400 |
| Label / tag | DM Sans | 12 / 16 | 700, `letter-spacing: 0.04em`, uppercase allowed here only |
| Dose number | DM Sans | 36 / 40 | 700, tabular-nums |

Body text is at least 16px. Nothing goes below 12px.

