## 5. Components

### Buttons

- Primary: coral background, ink text, pill shape, 52px tall, DM Sans 700 at 16px. Darken 8% when pressed.
- Secondary: transparent background, 2px ink border, ink text, pill shape.
- Text link: coral-deep, underlined on hover and focus.
- Destructive: danger-colored outline. Fill it only on the final confirmation step.
- Buttons are full-width on mobile. Focus ring is `0 0 0 3px var(--color-cobalt)` with a 2px offset.

### Cards

- White on cream (surface on bg in dark mode), 24px radius, 20 to 24px padding, 1px `--color-line` border.
- Hero cards for milestones and countdowns use a solid coral or sun background, ink text, and a large Bricolage number or headline.

### Tags and status chips

Pill shape using the label text style. Variants:

- neutral: line-colored background
- info: 12% cobalt tint with cobalt text
- success
- warning
- danger, for true alerts only

### Inputs

16px radius, 52px tall, 1.5px `--color-line` border, cobalt border on focus. Labels sit above the field and stay visible. Don't use placeholder text as the only label.

### Progress

Show cycle progress as a thick rounded bar or ring in coral on a line-colored track, with the day count in large tabular numerals.

### Bottom navigation (mobile)

Four or five items at most, for example Today, Cycle, Meds, Costs, Profile (adapt to the existing routes). The active item gets an ink icon and label with a small coral dot or pill indicator. The bar uses the surface color with a top border in the line color.

### Icons

Rounded icons in filled or duotone style (Phosphor "fill" or "duotone", or Lucide with a 2px stroke and rounded joins). Use an abstract droplet or pill shape for doses. No sharp clinical line art and no realistic needles or syringes.

### Motion

- UI transitions run 150 to 250ms with ease-out.
- Celebration animations appear in three places only: logging an injection (a quick scale and check), completing a stim day, and the retrieval countdown reaching zero. A small coral and sun burst is fine there.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.

