## 6. Imagery

- Photography is editorial, natural-light portraits of real, diverse people: different races, body types, ages 25 to 42, queer couples, single women, and cancer patients. They look styled, candid, and confident. Avoid smiling-doctor stock photos.
- Crop photos into rounded rectangles or circles, with a color-block shape behind or overlapping them.
- If there are no photos, use flat illustration in the palette: abstract cells and circles, sun and moon shapes for time and cycles, botanicals.
- Never use babies, pregnant bellies, realistic anatomy, needles or syringes, literal chicken eggs, or distressed imagery.
- Until real photography exists, use solid color blocks with a soft circle shape as placeholders. Don't pull random stock photos.

