## 8. Screens

Apply to whichever of these exist.

1. Welcome and onboarding. High energy. Full-bleed coral or sun hero, a large Bricolage headline (for example "Freeze your eggs on your schedule."), one circle motif, one photo, one pill CTA.
2. Today (home). A greeting, then a hero card with the cycle day in large tabular numerals and a progress bar. Below it, today's meds as calm white cards showing drug, dose in large numerals, time, and a "Log it" button. Then the next appointment card. One milestone card at most.
3. Cycle timeline. A vertical step list: Consult, Testing, Stim, Trigger, Retrieval, Freeze, Storage. Completed steps get an ink check, the current step a coral pill, upcoming steps ink-soft text. No decoration.
4. Medications and injection log. Calm mode: cream background, white cards, large dose numerals, clear times. Coral appears only on the "Log" button. Play the check animation when a dose is logged.
5. Monitoring and results. Calm mode. A plain-language summary at the top, then follicle sizes in a simple chart (cobalt bars or dots, labeled in mm). No red unless something is clinically urgent.
6. Trigger shot. The highest-precision screen: ink on white, a very large time display, a countdown, and a "Set alarm" button. No decoration.
7. Retrieval day. A countdown hero (sun background is fine) and a checklist covering fasting, a ride home, and arrival time. Results afterward go in a calm card.
8. Costs and billing. Calm mode. Itemize by payer (clinic, pharmacy, anesthesia, storage), show totals in large tabular numerals, and label each line with a status chip (Paid, Due, Estimate). Coral appears only on the "Pay" CTA.
9. Storage. One card showing eggs stored, location, renewal date, and annual fee.
10. Profile and settings. A standard list, including the dark mode toggle and the discreet notifications toggle.

